export function ethicsPolicy(){return `<div class="ethics-policy"><p class="intro-copy">Your roadmap belongs to you. AI suggests; you choose.</p><ol class="ethics-steps"><li><strong>Advice grounded in evidence.</strong><p>GoPlan combines your goals with reviewed AUI requirements and relevant research. You review proposed changes before they replace a saved plan. Course availability and individual approvals still need confirmation.</p></li><li><strong>A personal, private workspace.</strong><p>Your name, email, answers, roadmap and progress are stored for your account and synced across devices. The admin dashboard lists profile details and activity dates; it does not show your private roadmap, answers or grades.</p></li><li><strong>Clear limits.</strong><p>The AI can edit supported roadmap choices and semester placement. It cannot change university rules, dismiss validation warnings, receive attachments, contact others or complete official submissions. Unsupported requests leave your plan unchanged.</p></li></ol><details class="quiet-details"><summary>Storage, AI use and withdrawal</summary><h3>Account and storage</h3><p>GoPlan verifies your email when creating or recovering your account; later sign-ins use email and password. Your cloud profile and roadmaps remain until you delete them in Account → Privacy & account data. A browser copy helps recover unsynced edits. Signing out clears your account’s cached roadmaps on this browser; it does not delete cloud plans, older device-only plans or downloaded files.</p><h3>What the AI receives</h3><p>OpenAI receives your questionnaire, academic choices and relevant change requests. Later changes also include course codes, status and semester placement. Your name, sign-in email, exact GPA, grades and private progress notes are excluded from the automatic payload. A yes/no indicator of accelerated-load eligibility may be included. Anything you type into a request is sent as written, so avoid sensitive details. Public-topic research may supplement the reviewed academic data. OpenAI’s browser search uses Exa; only general topic queries are intended for search, with email addresses and phone numbers removed.</p><h3>Your included AI changes</h3><p>One roadmap includes two change prompts per guided stage and five global change prompts after saving. Submitted AI prompts use an allowance, including failed requests. Requests recognized locally as unsupported do not use an AI change. Private counters and response receipts enforce this across devices. Deleting your data removes response receipts; a hashed allowance record remains to prevent resets. Manual edits and Excel export stay available.</p><h3>What the dashboard measures</h3><p>The private dashboard shows registered names, emails, join dates and last account activity. Separately, it shows aggregate adviser outcomes, response time, provider usage, plan saves, accepted updates and Excel requests. Those counters contain no names or answers and do not measure unique visitors. Counters older than 90 days are deleted on the next measurement write.</p><h3>Your controls</h3><p>Account lets you edit your name, download your personal data, sign out or delete your GoPlan profile and cloud roadmaps. Authentication providers retain their own sign-in records under their policies. Authorized operators maintain the service; the student dashboard does not make your plan public.</p><a href="/privacy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full privacy notice</a></details></div>`;}
